"Authority control is the first step of magic: feeling one's authority and moving it deliberately."
"The beginner exercise needs a partner, who pats one's existence with authority to be patted back."
"Wizard-class Artonans do it naturally; Avowed normally cannot feel their own authority."
"Avowed use skills without learning magic because the Contract shapes their authority for them."
"Authority differs in quality, attachment and control; most improve with practice."
"A little willpower is needed to keep asserting authority when tired or depressed."
"Great presence, like the Primary's, can be felt by others."
